# print(sum([new Point(1, 2), new Point(3, 4)]));
# -- end of source
# f1 = lengthOf, f2 = sum
# A unit can be walked in three ways (walk/AOTMechanisms.h WayOfWalking): as built; with nothing carried (no callee copied in, nothing in front of loops, no tries of loops: a head claims nothing);
# closed (constants, direct calls and what callers left: every operation as the input has it). testing=WalksUnitsBy:<way>[:<n>:<seed>] forces a way on every unit that walks a body, or on one in n.
# RUN(ASBUILT): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# ASBUILT: frame 1 callee=f1
# ASBUILT: GetSlot {{*}} key="x"
# RUN(BARE): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=WalksUnitsBy:NothingCarried
# BARE-NOT: frame 1 callee=f1
# BARE: anything?LostByWalk @JSValue) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# BARE: GetArrayLength
# BARE: CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# RUN(CLOSED): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=WalksUnitsBy:Closed
# CLOSED-NOT: frame 1 callee=f1
# CLOSED: PropGet {{*}} key="length"
# CLOSED: ElemGet
# CLOSED: CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# CLOSED: Add {{*}} form=Generic
# What the unit has promised its callers it still gives: the result in its form, behind a test that stops.
# CLOSED: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=int|whole
# CLOSED: Return
# RUN(NOBODY): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=WalksUnitsBy:Closed:1000000:3
# NOBODY: frame 1 callee=f1
# Every way gives one answer.
# RUN(ANSWERBARE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=WalksUnitsBy:NothingCarried
# ANSWERBARE: 30
# RUN(ANSWERCLOSED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=WalksUnitsBy:Closed
# ANSWERCLOSED: 30
# RUN(ANSWERMIXED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=WalksUnitsBy:Closed:2:5
# ANSWERMIXED: 30
